#Lab Exercise 1: Sorting Products and Printing Prices using Playwright with Pytest
1. Open the Website
o Navigate to bstackdemo.com
2. Locate and Verify Dropdown
o Locate the "Order by" dropdown element.
o Assert that it is visible and enabled.
3. Sort Products
o Select the "Lowest to highest" option from the dropdown.
o Wait for the page to reflect the sorting changes.
4. Extract Product Data
o Capture all product prices and product names using locators:
▪ prices
▪ product names
5. Print Products and Prices
o Loop through all products and print names with corresponding prices.
6. Identify Lowest & Highest Priced Products
o Print the first product as the lowest priced
o Print the last product as the highest priced
Expected Output
• All product names and their prices printed in ascending order of price.
• Lowest-priced product printed first with its price.
• Highest-priced product printed last with its price.